{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>I did not [speak in secret, etc.]</b> Now, I did not create the earth for tohu; how, then, would I say to the seed of Israel, 'Seek Me in tohu'? Many interpreted 'I did not speak in secret' as referring to the assembly at Mount Sinai. What seems correct to me is that it alludes to these future things, the secret of which He revealed to His prophet, and His prophet to Israel and to the nations; therefore He said, 'declaring upright things [מגיד מישרים].'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "Resolved וגו' (etc.) by supplying the elliptical phrase from the verse lemma; added bracketed clarifier for the English reader since Ibn Ezra's lemma does not spell out the continuation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:14.519063277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}